course: dictionary
lesson: 4586
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words can mean more than one thing, and only the sentence tells you which meaning is meant. «The farmer grew hemp in the field.» Here hemp is a plant, because farmers grow plants in fields. Look at the other words around the word to find the clue.
explain: «The old ship used hemp rope to hold its sails.» Rope and sails tell you that hemp means the strong fibres of the plant, used to make things. Hemp can also mean the seeds or oil, as in «hemp seeds» or «hemp milk». Try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: In Mandarin Chinese, the way your voice rises and falls is part of the word. Mei hears «mā, má, mǎ, mà» as four different words: mother, hemp, horse and scold. Her friend hears only «ma» because the tone is missing, so listen to the whole sound, not just the letters.
fact: Hemp is a tall plant whose strong stem fibres are used to make rope, cloth and paper.
fact: The seeds and oil of hemp are used in food, and hemp is used in clothes and building.
fact: «Hemp seeds» and «hemp milk» are sold as food in shops.
fact: Hemp grows fast and is eco-friendly, so designers and scientists like using it.
fact: Hemp is a kind of cannabis plant, but the hemp used for rope and food has very little of the drug in it.
exercise: «The farmer grew hemp in the field.» In this sentence, what is hemp? | *A plant | A type of boat | A kind of tree | A coat
exercise: «The old ship used hemp rope and canvas for its sails.» What is hemp rope made from? | Melted sugar | Metal wire | *Strong fibres from the hemp plant | Seaweed
exercise: Mei hears «ma» but her teacher says «mā» and «má» are different words. Why? | Because she is speaking very loudly | Because the words are spelled differently on paper | Because her friend is not listening | *Because the rise and fall of the voice is part of the word
test: «Hemp seeds are sold as food in the shop.» What does this tell you about hemp? | *Parts of the hemp plant, such as its seeds, can be eaten | Hemp is a metal | Hemp grows only underwater | Hemp is only used to build roads
test: Why was hemp rope useful on old sailing ships? | *It was strong, so it could be used for ropes and sails | It melted in the sea | It was soft, like a feather | It was painted gold
exam: In which sentence does hemp mean the plant itself? | *«The hemp field was green and tall in the summer.» | «The hemp rope was thick and strong.» | «The hemp milk was cold and sweet.» | «Hemp seeds are sold as food.»
